from pathlib import Path
r=Path.cwd();p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');position=s.index('user_order = [')
chapters='''USER.append(('Inspect tables views and schemas', [
'Open the intended project or cache and choose Database schema in the upper-right page selector. A table stores rows, a view names a query result, and a schema qualifies object names. DPH shows what captured source declares or references; it does not connect to a database. Select a row to read its name, evidence state, schema qualifier, captured definition, source line, SHA256 and generation in the labeled evidence memo. Drag the divider below the list and scroll the memo for the full explanation.',
'Declared header means a supported CREATE TABLE, CREATE VIEW or CREATE SCHEMA header was captured in a referenced SQL resource with balanced parentheses. Its displayed definition omits comments and string literals. This establishes the captured declaration text, not valid body grammar, column or constraint semantics, deployed existence, privileges or database compatibility. Qualifier reference means a qualified object name mentions a schema; it does not establish CREATE SCHEMA. Inferred reference means the existing supported SQL analysis names an object whose table or view identity and definition are unverified. Unsupported statements remain visible as gaps.',
'Combine the object-kind selector, text filter and evidence-state selector to find a table, view, schema or unsupported statement. Text matches object names, qualifiers and source files. First page and Next page show up to 250 matches. In a narrow window, scroll the command strip sideways to reach the evidence-state selector and Open source. Open source requires attached, unchanged source from the same generation. Detached, changed, historical or outside-project source is refused with an explanation in the memo.',
'Multiple declarations with the same exact kind and spelling retain every definition and show a count. DPH does not choose a migration winner, merge dialect-specific identifier case, or infer deployment order. Ask the maintainer which approved scripts and migration sequence define the intended system. Empty results can mean missing resources or filters; they do not prove there is no schema. Referenced literal SQL files are discovered through existing project inventory rules. Original source and caches remain unchanged and can contain sensitive data. Full start, practice and developer directions are in docs/guides/Database_Schema_Run_and_Test.txt.'
]))
ENGINEERING.append(('Inspect captured database schema evidence', [
'DPH.Workspace.DatabaseSchema projects captured SQL resource IR and existing semantic SQL-table references without storage migrations or target execution. A bounded lexer separates comments, quoted identifiers and string literals, preserves statement-start lines, and recognizes supported CREATE TABLE, VIEW and SCHEMA headers. Qualified names retain quoted spelling; two- and three-part names yield qualifier-reference rows. PostgreSQL CREATE TABLE, CREATE VIEW and CREATE SCHEMA documentation provides header references, not a cross-dialect grammar guarantee. Unsupported headers, ALTER and other statements remain explicit gaps.',
'The lexer limits each resource to 2 MiB characters and 100000 tokens, nested comments to 16 levels and the inventory to 10000 rows. Malformed lexical resources yield a gap instead of partially promoted declarations. Definitions omit comment and string contents and bound display length. Parenthesis balance and recognized headers do not validate body grammar, type or constraint semantics. Whole-resource byte extents and precise statement-start lines are labeled separately. Existing inferred references retain captured semantic ranges and use original relationship labels for object names.',
'Exact kind and spelling index duplicate declarations projectwide; every captured definition remains visible and migration order remains unresolved. The inspector neither normalizes dialect-dependent identifiers nor selects an effective production definition. References stay distinct from declarations; schema qualifiers stay distinct from explicit schema declarations. Missing resources and unsupported constructs cannot establish an empty live schema.',
'DPH.UI.Main.fmx serializes the Database schema page, toolbar, filters, list, divider, labeled memo and source command for the IDE. Main owns the projection and borrows only visible rows, clearing them before capture replacement or destruction. Filtering and paging show 250 rows. Open source reuses TDPHKeyboardInspector.ReadSource for generation, containment, identity, decoding and SHA256 guards. No runtime controls or additional navigation helper are introduced.',
'Run tools/build-database-schema.cmd elevated. Focused checks cover declarations, qualified and quoted names, comments/literals, duplicate definitions, unsupported and malformed resources, bounds, inferred references, SQLite persistence, source guards, unchanged workspace/catalog/source, native filters, pagination, capture replacement and normal/compact PaintTo renders. Run existing engine regression and tools/build-wp0.cmd for app and serialized FMX binding. Fixed ignored bin/database-schema-validation holds controlled practice data. No target SQL, database driver or application is executed.'
]))
for chapters in (USER, ENGINEERING):
 for index, (heading, paragraphs) in enumerate(chapters):
  chapters[index]=(heading,[p.replace('334 requirement records remain incomplete','333 requirement records remain incomplete') for p in paragraphs])

'''
