p=r/'help/index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');section='''<section><h2>Inspect tables views and schemas</h2><p>Open the intended project or cache, choose <strong>Database schema</strong> in the upper-right selector, and select a row. Tables store rows, views name query results, and schemas qualify object names. The labeled memo shows captured definitions, source line, SHA256 and generation.</p><p>Use kind, name/source text and evidence-state filters together. First page and Next page show 250 matches. Scroll commands sideways in a narrow window to reach Open source. That command requires unchanged attached source from the same generation; failures explain how to proceed.</p><p>Declared header establishes captured CREATE text, with body grammar, columns, constraints and deployment unverified. Qualifier reference does not prove a schema declaration. Inferred reference does not prove a table or view definition. Unsupported statements remain gaps. Duplicate exact kind/spelling declarations remain separate; ask the maintainer for the approved migration order. Empty results do not prove no schema exists. Displayed definitions omit comments and literals; original source/cache can still contain sensitive data. DPH executes no SQL.</p><p>Full directions: <code>docs/guides/Database_Schema_Run_and_Test.txt</code>. Elevated developer validation: <code>tools/build-database-schema.cmd</code>.</p></section>''';assert '<h2>Inspect tables views and schemas</h2>' not in s;s=s.replace('</main>',section+'</main>');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
